FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** The original author wrote about 40% of today's lines and hasn't committed in six months. They aren't the whole risk, because the next-largest owner is a recent contributor whose lines are mostly mechanical. I'd call the bus factor 2 on paper and about 1 in practice. Only about 12 of the 33 contributors with surviving lines have committed in the last year.

I ran the busfactor script with `--dry-run --no-github`, so nothing was written. The script only produced the coarse CODEOWNERS output, so I also used `git blame` on the current tree.

**Who wrote the current 2,279 lines** (`git blame`, whitespace and moves ignored):

| Author | Lines | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Felix "xq" Queißner (five emails merged) | about 910+ | about 40% | 2026-04-16 |
| Wen Li | 552 | 24% | 2026-10 |
| jnagpaul | 188 | 8% | 2023-07 |
| Vincent Rischmann | 132 | 6% | 2025-03 |
| The other ~28 authors | the rest | each under 4% | various |

I grouped Felix's lines by name. The five emails are `mq32.de`, `masterq32.de`, `ib-queissner.de`, `random-projects.net` and one more. Counting by email alone makes him look like several smaller contributors. His count is approximate because I summed it by hand.

**If Felix stopped answering:**
- About 40% of the code would have no author left to ask. This includes the early core of the parser and the build setup.
- Several other authors have also gone quiet. jnagpaul's 188 lines come from a single 2023 burst, and Rischmann has been silent since March 2025. Together with Felix that is roughly half the codebase.
- The script's roster still counts Felix as active, because its window is 12 months and his last commit is about 6 months old. It also lists him, via `<email redacted>`, as a fallback owner. You should check that roster before trusting it. If he really is gone, the repo has no live fallback owner.

**Why "2 on paper" is closer to 1 in practice:**
- Wen Li's 552 lines come from only three commits in October 2026. One is a 508-line codepoint-width helper. Another is a move of the sources into `src/`.
- Those commits are new code and file moves rather than long familiarity with the whole library.
- Wen Li and Tobias Ek (also three commits, all from the last three weeks) are the only active people the script names as owners under `/src/`.
- Both are brand new to the project. Their expertise is thin, even though their share of the lines is large.

**Caveats:**
- Commit volume is only a proxy for who understands the code. Reviewers who never commit are invisible to it.
- The history has commit dates later than today's date of 2026-10-24, up to 2026-11-04. I didn't investigate this, but it affects any "recent" cutoff.
- I didn't build the HTML risk report or write `.github/CODEOWNERS`. I can do that if you want. I'd first confirm with you whether Felix and the two `fjord.example` authors are still active.
